# Who must approve a change before it can merge.
#
# The maintainer decides what the app does and means. Contributors report faults
# and test builds. Nothing a contributor writes, and nothing the agent opens on a
# contributor's behalf, may reach `testing` without the maintainer. That is how a
# design decision stays the maintainer's, even for contributors with write access.
#
# This file does nothing alone. The `testing-guard` and `main-guard` rulesets
# must have "require review from Code Owners" on, with one approving review. The
# maintainer is a bypass actor on both, so their own pull requests still merge.
# See docs/contributor-pipeline.md, "Who can merge".
* @ParkingSoman
